# ARCH-001
# HCGO Architecture Documentation Standard

## Purpose

This document defines the official architecture documentation standard for HCGO.

Every approved architectural artifact shall conform to this standard.

No architectural work becomes part of the Enterprise Baseline until it is documented as one of the approved artifact types defined below.

---

# Artifact Naming Standard

Every approved artifact consists of two identifiers.

```
<Type>-<Project>-<Sequence>

Example:

CG-EP-001
```

Where:

| Component | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| **Type** | Defines the type of architectural artifact. |
| **Project** | Identifies the architecture workstream. |
| **Sequence** | Sequential identifier within that project. |

Example:

```
CG-EP-001

CG = Constitutional Guardrail

EP = Enterprise Persistence

001 = First approved Constitutional Guardrail
```

---

