---

# Approved Artifact Types

Only the following artifact types may become part of the approved Enterprise Baseline.

| Prefix | Artifact Type | Purpose |
|---------|---------------|---------|
| **ARCH** | Architecture Standard | Governs architecture documentation standards. |
| **CG** | Constitutional Guardrail | Constitutional constraints that architecture may not violate. |
| **PR** | Project Rule | Governs how a specific architecture project is executed. |
| **DF** | Discovery Finding | Documents approved discovery outcomes. |
| **AF** | Analysis Finding | Documents approved analysis outcomes. |
| **ADR** | Architectural Decision Record | Records approved architectural decisions. |
| **PA** | Persistence Architecture | Defines the approved persistence architecture. |
| **IR** | Implementation Readiness | Documents implementation readiness and handoff. |

---

# Enterprise Baseline Rule

From this point forward, nothing becomes part of the approved Enterprise Baseline unless it is explicitly documented as one of the approved artifact types.

Working discussions are not architecture.

Only approved architectural artifacts become part of the official HCGO Enterprise Baseline.

---

# Architectural Lifecycle

```
Architecture Standard (ARCH)

        ↓

Constitutional Guardrails (CG)

        ↓

Project Rules (PR)

        ↓

Discovery Findings (DF)

        ↓

Analysis Findings (AF)

        ↓

Architectural Decision Records (ADR)

        ↓

Persistence Architecture (PA)

        ↓

Implementation Readiness (IR)

        ↓

Implementation
```

---

# Architectural Meaning

Architecture Standards establish how architecture is documented.

Constitutional Guardrails establish architectural boundaries.

Project Rules govern how architectural work is conducted.

Discovery identifies validated findings.

Analysis establishes architectural relationships.

Architectural Decisions record approved design decisions.

Persistence Architecture defines the approved enterprise architecture.

Implementation Readiness prepares architecture for implementation.

---

# Future Expansion

Additional project identifiers may be introduced as new HCGO enterprise architecture initiatives are approved.

The artifact type definitions established in this standard shall remain consistent across all HCGO architecture efforts unless formally revised.